From f0140e0000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 0140e] evergo: do not call into a NULL coalition

The v64 boot died in a data abort:

  panic(cpu 0 caller ...): Kernel data abort. at pc 0xfffffe000732407c,
      lr 0xfffffe0007324684, far 0x0 esr 0x96000006

sym_kernel.py resolves the pc to _i_coal_jetsam_set_taskrole + 0xf8, and
disassembling it shows the faulting instruction:

    ldr  x8, [x1, #0x5e0]      ; x8 = task->coalition[COALITION_TYPE_JETSAM]
    ldr  x9, [x8]              ; <- faults: x8 is NULL
    cmp  x9, x0

So task->coalition[JETSAM] is NULL and the code dereferences it.

0090e already made the jetsam set_taskrole mismatch non-fatal, but it only
checked the coalition *identity*:

    if (task->coalition[i] != coalitions[i]) { ...skip... }

That check passes when both sides are NULL - and then the code goes on to call
coal_call(coalitions[i], set_taskrole, ...), which dereferences the NULL
coalition. The kernel log shows the two cases mixed:

    coalitions_set_roles: pid 29 not a member of RESOURCE coalition id:17, skipping
    coalitions_set_roles: pid 29 not a member of JETSAM coalition id:18, skipping

so some types were skipped and one of them was NULL.

Skip NULL coalitions outright, and skip a task that has no coalition of that
type at all. A task without a role only loses that coalition's accounting; the
process still runs, which is what 0090e was after.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/coalition.c b/osfmk/kern/coalition.c
index cbfb2cc..e0f9ed3 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/coalition.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/coalition.c
@@ -1893,6 +1893,19 @@ coalitions_set_roles(coalition_t coalitions[COALITION_NUM_TYPES],
 		 * adopt it, and then the per-type set_taskrole would trip its
 		 * assertion and panic the kernel.
 		 */
+		if (coalitions[i] == COALITION_NULL) {
+			/*
+			 * evergo (0140e): a NULL coalition would be
+			 * dereferenced by coal_call() below.  The identity check
+			 * 0090e added does not catch this: it passes when the
+			 * task has no coalition of this type either, and the
+			 * call then faults on the NULL.
+			 */
+			printf("coalitions_set_roles: pid %d has no %s "
+			    "coalition, skipping\n", task_pid(task),
+			    coal_type_str(i));
+			continue;
+		}
 		if (task->coalition[i] != coalitions[i]) {
 			printf("coalitions_set_roles: pid %d not a member of %s "
 			    "coalition id:%llu, skipping\n", task_pid(task),
